  "scope": "Unchanged RSTimer, PersistTimer, TimerFlag, TimerManager, TimerRegistry and the fourteen engine timers of core/game/system/timer/impl (AntiMacro, Disease, DragonFireImmunity, Frozen, FrozenImmunity, HealOverTime, Miasmic, MiasmicImmunity, Poison, PoisonImmunity, SkillRestore, Skulled, SpellbookSwap, Teleblock), registered once each in the class scan's order through their own constructors, with the unchanged SpellBookManager, Event, EventHook, EquipmentSlot, Privilege, Globals and TickUtils, on JDK 11 with Kotlin 1.8.20, kotlin-reflect 1.6.10 (createInstance), JSON-simple 1.1.1 and the published ConstLib 1.4.28 (Sounds and Items values checked against the suffixes of the names used). Original text inserted into adapters at generation time: the ContentAPI timer, poison, level, equipment and attribute functions; Entity's hook map with its dispatch, unhook and hook bodies; Skills' constants, lastTrainedSkill/lastXpGain and heal, updateLevel, getStaticLevel, getLevel, getMaximumLifepoints, getLifepoints and getEntity; Settings' special energy field, getter and setter; Player's logout listener map; RandomFunction.random(a, b) and random(max); the Log, Rights, PrayerType, ZoneRestriction and HitsplatType constants; Location.toString; the five hooked event declarations and their core.api.Event constants; the RandomEvents constant names with their loot and type arguments. Everything else is a recording adapter answering from the case: ticks, names, locations, script delay and weak scripts, modal state, debug messages, rights, artificial flag, uid lookups, slayer tasks, familiar owners, manualHit, skill packets, the damage-sponge perk, assist sessions (always absent), equipment, varps and varbits, messages, audio, skull icon and state, tabs, the weapon interface extension and its selectAutoSpell, autocast spell presence, attributes, poison immunity, zone restriction, dialogue ids, logout listener registration, logging, the random event pool, event NPC creation, spawn location, init, terminate and loot. RandomFunction.RANDOM is a seeded recording java.util.Random. Printed stack traces are recorded by exception class. Not driven: AntiMacro.defineCommands (the ::revent command), the random event content, farming/other content timers, the world tick loop and Entity.init/finalizeDeath.",
